# SeismoNet .gitignore — see docs/REPRODUCIBILITY.md §10.3 and docs/TECHNICAL_ARCHITECTURE.md §11
# Rationale for every section is given in the heading comment.
# This file was created before any dataset, checkpoint, or generated artifact existed,
# so that large or sensitive files can never be committed by accident (R-16, FR-048).

# ── Virtual environments (reproducibility: environments are declared via a lockfile and rebuilt, not committed)
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# ── Python bytecode and caches (generated, never curated)
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
.coverage
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
*.cover

# ── Dependency and build artifacts (resolved from the lockfile, not stored)
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
*.whl
frontend/node_modules/

# ── Secrets and local configuration (must never be committed — NFR-015)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets/
*secret*
*token*
*.token

# ── Raw and interim datasets (large, licence-restricted, and re-obtainable — NFR-009, DR-005/DR-006)
# The dataset is not bundled with the repo; it is downloaded per DATASET_GUIDE.md.
data/raw/
data/interim/
data/cache/
*.hdf5
*.h5
*.mseed
*.sac
*.mseed.gz
*.sac.gz

# ── Processed / derived data (regenerable from raw + config)
data/processed/

# ── Train/validation/test split files — EXCEPTION
# Split files are small, diff-able, and part of the result (FR-005, SC-8),
# so they ARE tracked. Only large derived splits would be ignored:
# (no ignore rule for splits/*.csv — keep them)

# ── Model checkpoints and training artefacts (large binaries; weights-only in safetensors — FR-046)
models/
checkpoints/
*.safetensors
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.bin
runs/*
lightning_logs/

# ── Generated results, figures, and reports output (regenerable via FR-078)
results/
reports/generated/
*.png.bak

# ── Logs
*.log
logs/

# ── OS and editor artefacts (local, not project content)
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/settings.json
.vscode/*.code-workspace
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace

# ── Jupyter checkpoints
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ── Demo artefacts required to run the web app from a clean clone — EXCEPTION
# The rules above ignore training output, and they still do. But the frozen checkpoint, the frozen
# protocol, the config snapshot, the run manifests and the held-out test metrics are *inputs* to the
# demonstration, not regenerated output: without them `backend.main` cannot even import (the engine
# loads the checkpoint at startup) and the Model Evaluation page returns 503. The subset below is
# ~2.9 MB in total and makes `git clone` → run work. Everything else under runs/ stays ignored.
# `runs/` had to become `runs/*` for these negations to apply, because Git cannot re-include a file
# whose parent directory is excluded.
!runs/experiment_002_p_training/
runs/experiment_002_p_training/*
!runs/experiment_002_p_training/best.pt
!runs/experiment_002_p_training/run.json
!runs/validation_protocol_candidate_seed42/
runs/validation_protocol_candidate_seed42/*
!runs/validation_protocol_candidate_seed42/protocol.json
!runs/pilot_seed42/
runs/pilot_seed42/*
!runs/pilot_seed42/run.json
!runs/pilot_seed42/config_snapshot.yaml
!runs/eval_test_best/
runs/eval_test_best/*
!runs/eval_test_best/metrics.json
!runs/validation_inference_p6_seed42/
runs/validation_inference_p6_seed42/*
!runs/validation_inference_p6_seed42/predictions.json

